{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2536 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "bee2aea02a54308169e5be9b3e91a5cc8c7ca3cd204a158e2670b96786eec913" :edb/db-before-t 2535 :edb/db-after-t 2536 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535848 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:53:18.608Z" 13194139535848 true] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369975 13194139535848 true] [17592186184108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369996 13194139535848 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369968 13194139535848 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369982 13194139535848 true] [17592186184137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186369989 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369969 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1089 "q-106930" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1100 "Let $L$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=ax+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1113 #uuid "15beea94-47dc-575a-be81-e2d3b2547e2f" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369968 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)=x+1,$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2x+2.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin L$ because the constant term is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in L.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of real valued functions satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369970 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369971 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369972 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369973 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369974 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1041 "selection" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369971 13194139535848 true] [17592186369969 1110 #uuid "1be1f1ff-185c-5903-841f-0172a0c5e527" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369970 1034 "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in L$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369970 1111 #uuid "08f26cd7-b4e2-533f-9258-7e760fd6f507" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369971 1034 "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369971 1111 #uuid "a664ff91-48f1-5ae4-ada4-3fa4b166eb07" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369972 1034 "addition of functions in $L$ is not associative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369972 1111 #uuid "07f60e7f-6e02-5f1c-b720-366aa10a0075" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369973 1034 "addition of functions in $L$ is not commutative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369973 1111 #uuid "22a4e1ec-05fc-513a-bbbb-196e2f363402" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369974 1034 "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369974 1111 #uuid "02790ff3-06cd-5da0-9e4b-98da0a0d0833" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369976 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1089 "q-106940" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $y$ and $z$ are vectors such that $x+y=z+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $y=z.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1113 #uuid "01cc4fec-23d5-5237-aea5-3e56464042be" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369975 1145 "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369977 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369978 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369979 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369980 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369981 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1041 "selection" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369980 13194139535848 true] [17592186369976 1110 #uuid "4e95976d-6212-5c03-ba82-7f260ee5e5e3" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369977 1034 "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A5}$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369977 1111 #uuid "3638f7b7-802a-5b50-aa15-d0eaadee0ff1" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369978 1034 "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369978 1111 #uuid "cf08fb6b-e3b2-5444-b00f-2d86b3d4ef55" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369979 1034 "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A5}$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369979 1111 #uuid "85ad6021-1111-585d-ba15-9f99f5bc0e48" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369980 1034 "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369980 1111 #uuid "15d8720c-d1e6-54d7-95d2-a4a228ee7476" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369981 1034 "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369981 1111 #uuid "ae72d013-20aa-5576-9391-4efcb759de85" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369983 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1089 "q-94807" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1100 "Let $K$ be the set of all $2\\times 1$ matrices $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],$ such that $x,y\\in R$ and $x+y=1.$  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1113 #uuid "4e9325bc-24c1-5d82-b1cc-1e1fb76a771a" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369982 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$** *  \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,✓$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369984 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369985 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369986 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369987 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369988 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1041 "selection" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369986 13194139535848 true] [17592186369983 1110 #uuid "2ec4fdc0-c432-52d0-af9b-88539b8e2fc9" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369984 1034 "addition and scalar multiplication of matrices do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369984 1111 #uuid "33bc630d-d0c0-5066-b1ce-17330dcdabf2" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369985 1034 "$1\\cdot A\\ne A$ for all $A\\in K$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369985 1111 #uuid "531c2d53-e212-5909-8ba9-484863df4a59" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369986 1034 "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369986 1111 #uuid "31989510-9ee3-533e-ba1e-dbaada39a136" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369987 1034 "addition of matrices is not commutative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369987 1111 #uuid "e822e1fc-9467-5db2-b2b9-2e54f6438e1a" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369988 1034 "addition of matrices is not associative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369988 1111 #uuid "6a1eb1df-2deb-5d1e-ad76-5ace4dce98f0" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369990 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1089 "q-94808" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1100 "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1113 #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369989 1145 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369991 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369992 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369993 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369994 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369995 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1041 "selection" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369992 13194139535848 true] [17592186369990 1110 #uuid "a0c74e80-66a0-5e58-b9e1-e1d5d2a42b4e" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369991 1034 "addition in $Y$ is not associative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369991 1111 #uuid "aea792ce-4a6e-5721-9a18-f99292949277" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369992 1034 "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369992 1111 #uuid "dc50024b-9085-5119-8f2d-a8ca14bd95e7" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369993 1034 "$Y$ does not contain the zero element" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369993 1111 #uuid "93950d71-49ab-5d0d-979c-95c7a0e6b532" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369994 1034 "addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$  do not satisfy the distributive laws" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369994 1111 #uuid "c6f8dea0-a011-58db-a415-7ee98ad9d04d" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369995 1034 "addition in $Y$ is not commutative" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535848 true] [17592186369995 1111 #uuid "171a1a9b-b707-5744-b4d1-6b9dfc2d920f" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369997 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1089 "q-94937" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1100 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1113 #uuid "f54d0d72-c3d0-5096-886c-e29b889e3841" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369996 1145 "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A1\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A4\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369998 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369999 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370000 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370001 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370002 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1041 "selection" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369998 13194139535848 true] [17592186369997 1110 #uuid "a501bedf-1c70-5820-92cf-3a7a11f55678" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369998 1034 "\\text{A1},\\text{A4}" 13194139535848 true] [17592186369998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535848 true] [175921863